'''Pretty Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked during the [[Castle & Dragon Collaboration Event]] by completing the stage [[For Pretty Cat]] with a [[Timed Score Reward|Timed Score]] of at least 4,500. She was added in [[Version 4.6 Update|Version 4.6]]. [[True Form]] also added in Version 4.6 improved the chance to [[Freeze]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 254
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Pretty Cat
|name2 = Lovely Pretty Cat
|name3 = Cyber Pretty Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Lovely Pretty Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cyber Pretty Cat''' when obtained from the [[Road to Pretty Cat Evolution (Normal)|Road to Pretty Cat Evolution]] stage and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Pretty Cat is a poor man's [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat]] to put it nicely. She has incredibly low range, stats, Freeze chance and Freeze uptime, with the cherry on top being Single Attack. This adds up to mean that she can only really work against melee enemies such as [[Bore]] or certain [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclones]] when supported with other crowd-controllers. Her True Form may double her chance to Freeze, but that only takes it from offensively bad to just bad.

Outside of certain Castle & Dragon stages that only allow the use of the Collab's units, there are many Cats out there capable of Freezing who also don't have to deal with all of Pretty Cat's flaws. [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]], [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] are all wonderful examples. Given that she can't even do Healer's job cheesing stages, Pretty Cat is better off forgotten.

